    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This case study explores the relationship between reducing the academic achievement gap and educational resources in the local governments of Japan. Two prefectures were selected as successful examples of reducing the gap based on the results of the National Academic Survey from 2013 to 2022. Data included prefecture-produced documents, questionnaires, and interviews with policymakers. The findings reveal that policymakers in both prefectures recognized the problems related to student underachievement in their prefectures and thus implemented various measures designed to improve student outcomes. Furthermore, they allocated five common educational resources they thought would be effective: prefecture-level academic achievement tests, support for school management, additional teachers for proficiency-based classes, support for teachers’ pedagogy, and support for students’ supplemental learning. According to previous studies, many of those educational resources support the realization of “effective schools.”",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Suzuki, R. (2024). The Role of Educational Resources in Reducing the Academic Achievement Gap: A Case Study of Japanese Local Governments. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/sb041tk2855. https://doi.org/10.25740/sb041tk2855.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
    ],
